2040..2117 Comment "/// The three laws together. Associativity\'s inner `ext(m, k)` is an instance"
2118..2185 Comment "/// of its own left side and of both unit laws\', and its right side"
2186..2253 Comment "/// substitutes `k` under `bind x .`: each pair is found by pattern"
2254..2313 Comment "/// unification, and its two reducts normalize to one term."
